# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES R12 — A `raw/1` APPEARS IN THE NOTES RENDER PATH
# (ADR-053 §6 R12; WS-Notes Phase 3 gate P3). `PageLive`'s legacy-body branch stops going through
# the constrained inline renderer and hands the stored column straight to `Phoenix.HTML.raw/1`.
# Stored text is now MARKUP: an author-typed `<script>` is emitted as a live element, and the
# dialect is bypassed entirely. This is the one rendering shortcut ADR-053 §2 D3 forbids — the
# block editor stores text, so the page must never interpret it as HTML.
#
# Aimed at the render path only: `Samen.Web.Notes.Inline` (the tokeniser and its constructed HEEx),
# `Reads` (the plane-correct resolution), the write seam and every masking assertion are untouched,
# so exactly one test flips — the legacy-body proof that asserts stored text stays escaped text.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_surface_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a legacy body renders read-only through the inline renderer and can never become markup
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/page_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/page_live.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/page_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/page_live.ex
@@ -358,7 +358,3 @@
               <div class="note-legacy-body" id="note-legacy-body">
-                <%= if is_binary(@page.legacy.text) do %>
-                  {Samen.Web.Notes.Inline.render(@page.legacy.text)}
-                <% else %>
-                  {@page.legacy.text}
-                <% end %>
+                <%= Phoenix.HTML.raw(@page.legacy.text) %>
               </div>
